    "narrative": "For LawDog today, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (78.65) stands as the premier start, benefiting from a soft matchup against Martinez. While the platoon splits against right-handed pitching normally drag his ceiling down slightly, the raw volume provided by his #2 spot in the lineup and his recent sustained performance outweighs the matchup variables. **Jonathan Aranda** (67.38) remains our second essential play, capitalizing on a favorable encounter with Armstrong. The projection model likes the synergy of his #2 order placement and the 4.35 xERA of the opposing starter, suggesting a high probability for counting stat production, particularly in the Runs and RBI categories which remain vital for our 5x5 standing.\n\nWith the majority of our heavy hitters like **Bryce Harper**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Yainer Diaz** sidelined by a team-wide off-day, we are essentially forced into a limited roster configuration. The scarcity of our speed-threat assets like **Justin Crawford**, **Dylan Beavers**, and **Masyn Winn** is mitigated by the fact that they aren't active today, meaning we must rely on the floor stability provided by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Jonathan Aranda**. Looking further down the depth chart, the decision to leave players like **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Braden Montgomery** inactive was simple, as they all share the same lack of game opportunity today. The primary risk to monitor is any late-breaking lineup volatility for **Jonathan Aranda**; should he be shifted down the order, his score would experience a non-trivial decline, though given the current landscape, he remains a locked-in asset for this rotation.",
